<code>assert this.size() == \result.size() && \forall E e; this.contains(e) <=> ((HashSet<E>) \result).contains(e);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result.size() == this.size() && \forall E e; this.contains(e); ((HashSet<E>)\result).contains(e);</code>

This assert statement checks two conditions:
1. The size of the cloned set (`\result`) is equal to the size of the original set (`this`).
2. For every element `e` in the original set (`this`), the cloned set also contains `e`. 

Note that since we are dealing with sets, checking that both sets have the same size and that all elements of the original set are in the cloned set is sufficient to prove that the sets are equal.
--------------------
<code>assert this.equals(\result);</code>
